e someone might need W6 for a Chow. But if I keep it, I can form the Chow if I get another W6 or W8. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, Play B7. I have one B7. Since B7 has 2 left, maybe it's safe to discard. But B7 is a middle tile. If someone has B6 or B8, they might need it. But looking at the unshown tiles, B6 has 2 left. Not sure.\n\nWait, my meld is [W2, W3, W4], which is in Characters. Maybe I should focus on forming more Chows in the same suit. But I have W6, W7, W8. If I can form a Chow of W6-W7-W8, that would be good. But I need to keep those tiles. So if I discard any of them, I might break that possibility. So maybe it's better to keep W6, W7, W8 and not discard them. So among the valid actions, the ones to avoid discarding are W6, W7, W8.\n\nLooking at the valid actions again: Play T5, W6, W4, T8, W8, W7, B7, T1, T6, T9, T4.\n\nIf I discard T5, I lose a tile that could be part of T4-T5-T6 Chow. If I discard T5, then I can't form that Chow. So maybe better to keep T5. Similarly, T4 is part of that Chow. So if I discard T4, that would also break it. So I should avoid discarding T4 or T5 or T6 if possible.\n\nLooking at the other options: Play T8. I have T8 in my hand. If I discard T8, it's a terminal. Maybe someone is waiting for it. But I have only one T8. If I discard it, I can't form a pair. But maybe it's a safer discard since terminals are less likely to be part of a Chow. However, since I have T8 and T9, maybe keeping T8 for a possible pair later.\n\nPlay T1. Similarly, T1 is a terminal. If I discard it, maybe someone is waiting for it. But again, I have only one.\n\nPlay B7. B7 is a middle tile. If I discard it, maybe someone needs it for a Chow. But I don't have other B tiles except B7. So maybe safer to discard B7.\n\nSo between the options, maybe B7 is the safest to discard. Let's check the unshown tiles for B7: B7 has 2 left. So if I discard it, there are still some left. And since I don't have other B tiles to form a Chow or Pung, it's probably not useful